window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-2c6e218368c091d9"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"record-replay\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">录制与回放</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需完整的文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 后添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>“录制与回放”功能仅在 macOS 上提供；同时还必须能够使用并启用 Computer Use。</p> <p>“录制与回放”可以让你在 Mac 上演示某个工作流程，并将它转换为可重复使用的技能。当工作流程重复发生、依赖你的个人偏好，或者演示比文字描述更容易时，可以使用此功能。</p> <p>例如，你可以录制如何提交费用报销、预订停车位、创建配置正确的问题单、发布视频，或下载定期报告。ChatGPT 或 Codex 可以将这些操作模式整理成技能，供你之后通过 Computer Use、浏览器操作、已连接的插件或它们的组合再次使用。</p> <p><a id=\"before-you-start\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">开始之前</h2> <p>先选定一个你已经熟悉的工作流程。当步骤稳定且成功标准清晰时，“录制与回放”的效果最好。</p> <p><a id=\"start-a-recording\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">开始录制</h2> <ol> <li>在 ChatGPT 桌面应用中，选择 ChatGPT 并在切换器中启用 Work，或者选择 Codex。然后打开 <strong>Plugins（插件）</strong>。</li> <li>打开 <strong>+</strong> 菜单。</li> <li>选择 <strong>Record a skill（录制技能）</strong>。</li> <li>检查建议的提示词，补充有用的上下文，然后提交。</li> <li>当聊天请求录制你操作的权限时，等你准备好演示工作流程后再批准。</li> <li>在 Mac 上执行这个工作流程。</li> <li>完成后，从菜单栏或浮层中停止录制，或者告诉聊天你已经完成。</li> </ol> <p>录制期间，ChatGPT 或 Codex 会观察学习该工作流程所需的操作和窗口内容。录制会持续到你停止为止。请只演示你希望技能学会的任务。</p> <p>停止录制后，ChatGPT 或 Codex 会检查捕获到的工作流程并起草一个技能。技能会说明适用场景、所需输入、操作步骤以及如何验证结果。你也可以继续要求它修改完善。</p> <p><a id=\"replay-the-workflow\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">回放工作流程</h2> <p>开启一个新的 ChatGPT 或 Codex 聊天，并要求它使用生成的技能。提供这次与上次不同的值，例如要上传的文件、要创建的问题单或报告的日期范围。</p> <p>产品会把该技能作为可重复使用的上下文，然后使用当前环境中可用的工具完成工作流程，包括 Computer Use、浏览器操作和已安装的插件。</p> <p><a id=\"tips-for-better-recordings\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">提高录制效果的技巧</h2> <ul> <li>演示要简短且完整。</li> <li>开始前说明目标，以及可能变化的具体输入。</li> <li>使用真实的输入，但不要包含密钥等秘密或敏感信息。</li> <li>完成录制后，进一步说明重要但不易察觉的偏好，例如命名约定、默认值或决策点。</li> <li>工作流程完成后就停止录制，不要继续录制无关的整理操作。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"when-to-build-another-plugin\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">何时应改为构建插件</h2> <p>如果要在团队中分发独立且稳定的软件包、捆绑多项技能、加入连接器或 MCP 服务器，或者管理插件元数据，可以把工作流程打包为单独的插件。请参阅<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/plugins.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">构建插件</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"troubleshooting\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">故障排除</h2> <p><a id=\"i-dont-see-record-replay\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_8\">看不到“录制与回放”</h3> <p>如果组织使用 <code>requirements.toml</code> 管理 Codex，则 <code>[features].computer_use</code> 配置项也控制“录制与回放”。将 <code>computer_use = false</code> 写入该配置项会使这两项功能都不可用。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"record-replay\">Record &amp; Replay</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Record &amp; Replay is available on macOS. Computer Use must also be available and enabled.</p> <p>Record &amp; Replay lets you demonstrate a workflow on your Mac and turn it into a reusable skill. Use it when the workflow is repetitive, depends on your preferences, or is easier to show than to describe in a prompt.</p> <p>For example, you might record how you file an expense, book a parking space, create a correctly configured issue, publish a video, or download a recurring report. ChatGPT or Codex can package the pattern into a skill that you can use again with Computer Use, browser actions, connected plugins, or a combination of them.</p> <h2 id=\"before-you-start\">Before you start</h2> <p>Pick a workflow that you already know how to complete. Record &amp; Replay works best when the steps are stable and the success criteria are clear.</p> <h2 id=\"start-a-recording\">Start a recording</h2> <ol> <li>In the ChatGPT desktop app, select ChatGPT and turn on Work in the switcher, or select Codex. Then open <strong>Plugins</strong>.</li> <li>Open the <strong>+</strong> menu.</li> <li>Select <strong>Record a skill</strong>.</li> <li>Review the suggested prompt, add any helpful context, and submit it.</li> <li>When the chat asks for permission to record your actions, approve the request once you are ready to demonstrate the workflow.</li> <li>Perform the workflow on your Mac.</li> <li>When you are done, stop recording from the menu bar or overlay, or tell the chat that you are done.</li> </ol> <p>During recording, ChatGPT or Codex observes the actions and window content needed to learn the workflow. Recording continues until you stop it. Keep the recording focused on the task you want the skill to teach.</p> <p>After you stop recording, ChatGPT or Codex inspects the captured workflow and drafts a skill. The skill explains when to use the workflow, what inputs it needs, what steps to follow, and how to verify the result. You can also ask for further refinements.</p> <h2 id=\"replay-the-workflow\">Replay the workflow</h2> <p>Start a new ChatGPT or Codex chat and ask it to use the generated skill. Give it the values that are different this time, such as the file to upload, the issue to create, or the date range for the report.</p> <p>The product uses the skill as reusable context for the task. It can then complete the workflow with the tools available in the current environment, including Computer Use, browser actions, and installed plugins.</p> <h2 id=\"tips-for-better-recordings\">Tips for better recordings</h2> <ul> <li>Keep the demonstration short and complete.</li> <li>State your goal and any specific inputs that might vary between skill uses before you start recording.</li> <li>Use realistic inputs, but avoid secrets and sensitive data.</li> <li>Refine the skill after recording to call out hidden preferences that matter, such as naming conventions, field defaults, or decision points.</li> <li>Stop recording when the workflow is complete instead of continuing into unrelated cleanup.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"when-to-build-another-plugin\">When to build another plugin</h2> <p>Record &amp; Replay is a fast way to create a skill from a demonstrated workflow. If you want to distribute a separate stable package across a team, bundle multiple skills, include connectors, add MCP servers, or manage install metadata, package that workflow as its own plugin. See <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/plugins.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build plugins</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"troubleshooting\">Troubleshooting</h2> <h3 id=\"i-dont-see-record-replay\">I don't see Record &amp; Replay</h3> <p>If your organization manages Codex with <code>requirements.toml</code>, the <code>[features].computer_use</code> requirement controls Record &amp; Replay too. Setting <code>computer_use = false</code> makes both features unavailable.</p>"};
